menu "Regression tests"

config CONF_WITH_REGRESSION_TESTS
    bool "Include built-in regression tests"
    default y
    help
      Build the regression test harness into a separate HD image.
      When enabled, 'make test-hd' produces a raw disk image that
      boots pTOS and runs the test suite automatically.

config CONF_WITH_X86_64_MEMTEST
    bool "Run the x86-64 memory-management self-test at boot"
    depends on MACHINE_PC_X86_64
    default y
    help
      At every boot, exercise the tracked process allocations, the
      growable kernel heap, per-process address spaces and KPROC records
      with repeated create/exit and injected-failure cycles, and check that
      none of them leaks (bios/machine/pc-x86_64/memtest.c).  The result is
      one line on the console, "x86-64 memtest: PASS" or "FAIL (n)", which
      the CI boot test looks for.  It takes a fraction of a second.

endmenu
